# NL Native harness rules

This repo is a development harness, not an app. See [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md) and [CLAUDE.md](mdc:CLAUDE.md) for full context.

## No application code in this repo

- Never add Swift, Kotlin, or backend application sources at the top level.
- Never add platform build files (`Package.swift`, `build.gradle`, `Cargo.toml`, etc.).
- Worked examples in [example/](mdc:example) may contain spec artifacts, but not actual platform code.

## Agent ownership boundaries

- Each agent file in [agents/](mdc:agents) declares what it owns. Do not blur boundaries.
- Platform agents (iOS, Android, Backend) MUST NOT reference each other or each other's outputs. All cross-cutting decisions route through the Architect.
- Only the Architect bumps API contract or data model versions. Patch = cosmetic, Minor = additive, Major = breaking.
- The QA Verifier writes findings into a verification report. It never edits implementation files.
- The Spec Analyst never writes code and never picks technologies.

## EARS notation

All requirements in feature specs use EARS:

- `When [trigger], the system shall [behavior]`
- `While [state], the system shall [behavior]`
- `If [condition], then the system shall [behavior]`
- `The system shall [behavior]` (ubiquitous)

Don't write requirements as free-form prose.

## Spec versioning

- API contracts and data models in [schemas/](mdc:schemas) carry a semver version.
- Platform task lists declare contract dependencies in frontmatter. If a contract changes mid-implementation, dependent agents halt, re-read, reassess, and resume.

## Two-phase verification

- Phase A: per-platform spec compliance (parallel across iOS, Android, Backend).
- Phase B: cross-platform coherence + integration. Only runs if Phase A passes with no BLOCKERs.
- BLOCKER findings halt progress. WARNING findings are acknowledged but don't block.

## When you change something

- Touched an agent's role summary? Update [README.md](mdc:README.md).
- Touched an agent's key rule? Update [CLAUDE.md](mdc:CLAUDE.md) and [AGENTS.md](mdc:AGENTS.md).
- Added a slash command? Update the command tables in README, CLAUDE, and AGENTS.
- Added a schema? Update the schema lists in all three docs.
